 "insultsIntro": "1 Henry VI is full of abuse across the Channel and inside the English court. Talbot calls Joan witch, strumpet and 'Pucelle or puzzel'; Gloucester and Winchester trade 'peel'd priest' and 'proditor' at the Tower gates; Somerset and Plantagenet turn a legal quarrel into 'yeoman' and 'peevish boy'; and Joan, captured, curses her own father. The insults map the play's two wars, the one with France and the one beginning at home.",
